WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.890
A Quiet Place has triumphantly tiptoed into
theaters, enjoying critical acclaim as well

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.850
as success at the box office.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.990
Director John Krasinski delivers a thriller
with a unique concept and a cleverly limited

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.500
set of cinematic tools.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.010
Unlike most modern mainstream movies, it's
a film that relies less on spoken dialogue

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.740
than on ambient sounds, visuals, and mystery.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.940
A Quiet Place introduces the Abbott family,
who try to survive on their secluded farm

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.430
after a worldwide invasion of creatures that
hunt by sound.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:32.439
Getting by with a variety of creative sound-dampening
solutions and communicating with sign language,

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.160
they face the challenges of adolescence, guilt,
and even a pregnancy.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.160
Their story builds to a climax that wraps
up the action while leaving a few questions

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.180
still unanswered.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.880
If you want to know more about just what went
down in the final minutes, keep quiet and

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.129
check out our spoiler-filled rundown.

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:50.360
This the ending of A Quiet Place explained.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.929
Rockets' red glare

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:56.000
In A Quiet Place's opening scene, youngest
child Beau proposes that a rocketship could

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.410
help the family escape.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.850
His fascination with space travel proves to
be his downfall, as a toy shuttle in his hands

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.790
makes enough electronic noise to attract one
of the creatures.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.390
His family watches helplessly as the boy is
snatched away just before the main title.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.470
Beau's death informs the character arcs for
the rest of the story, as the film jumps ahead

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.480
a year and finds everyone struggling with
grief and guilt while attempting to maintain

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.480
some sense of normalcy under the oppressive
silence.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.060
His memory plays a key role in the finale,
as the monsters move in on Evelyn Abbott when

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.120
she goes into labor.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.410
Her husband, Lee and their son, Marcus draw
them away by putting into action a one-word

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:31.860
plan: "Rockets."

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.500
While the farm glows red with the warning
lights that signal an attack, a volley of

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.570
fireworks distracts the beasts and allows
Lee to take back the house and rejoin his

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.450
wife and newborn son.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.990
Sacrificial scream

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.530
One of A Quiet Place's central plot threads
focuses on Lee and Evelyn's daughter, Regan,

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.030
and her strained relationship with her father.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:53.740
As the one who gave Beau the toy that led
to his death, Regan thinks that Lee blames

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.740
her.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.360
Lee's overprotective tendencies toward his
deaf daughter don't exactly help her feel

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.860
that he believes in her, either.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.960
In one of the film's key scenes, Marcus reminds
his father that he needs to tell Regan how

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.030
much he loves her.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:09.209
It is a huge emotional payoff, then, when
Lee rescues Marcus and Regan from a creature

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:11.090
and tells them that he has always loved them.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.769
While the kids take shelter inside a pickup
truck with the beast clawing to get inside,

00:02:14.769 --> 00:02:18.970
Lee lets out one final, anguished scream,
giving his life to save them as they throw

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:21.630
the truck into neutral and it rolls back to
the house.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:25.780
It's a cathartic moment not only for the three
characters, but for the audience as well,

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.620
to break the silence with a tragic but triumphant
emotional release.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.450
All ears

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.739
The greatest mystery of A Quiet Place remains
the creatures themselves.

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:38.879
Aside from some vague news headlines, there
is barely any exposition given about where

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:41.329
they come from or just how the invasion went
down.

00:02:41.329 --> 00:02:46.060
For most of the film's runtime, the monsters
are glimpsed only briefly, appearing as fleeting

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.719
blurs or vague shapes.

00:02:47.719 --> 00:02:51.860
The climax, however, finally reveals them
in all their gruesome glory as one of them

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.609
stalks Evelyn and her newborn baby into the
basement of the farmhouse.

00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:59.999
They have eyeless heads that splits open in
all directions to expose sensitive hearing

00:02:59.999 --> 00:03:00.999
membranes.

00:03:00.999 --> 00:03:05.299
In addition to delivering a horrific visual,
this design explains the physiology that allows

00:03:05.299 --> 00:03:09.109
the beasts to so accurately strike at even
the subtlest sounds.

00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:10.499
Ferocious feedback

00:03:10.499 --> 00:03:15.090
A unique aspect of A Quiet Place is its use
of American Sign Language to convey the vast

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.430
majority of the dialogue.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:20.529
Krasinski chose to hire a deaf actress to
portray the hearing-impaired Regan for the

00:03:20.529 --> 00:03:24.680
sake of authenticity, and he worked with her
to develop signing habits and styles that

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.859
informed each family member's attitude and
character arc.

00:03:27.859 --> 00:03:31.700
The monsters' weakness is at last revealed
to be feedback, as the noise emitted from

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:35.689
Regan's cochlear implant when they are near
confuses their heightened sense and racks

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:36.689
them with pain.

00:03:36.689 --> 00:03:41.840
During the final confrontation, Regan discovers
the pile of discarded custom boosted implants

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.739
that Lee had been working on, showing how
much he cared for her while also providing

00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:48.969
her with the ability to fight back for the
first time.

00:03:48.969 --> 00:03:50.400
Locked and loaded

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.599
Regan uses Lee's radio transmitter to amplify
the feedback, causing the intruder to recoil,

00:03:55.599 --> 00:03:58.450
disoriented, and expose its inner membranes.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.299
Evelyn takes the opportunity of having a clear
shot at this weak spot for the first time

00:04:02.299 --> 00:04:05.110
and blows the thing away with her shotgun.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.829
Naturally, this is the kind of loud sound
the Abbots have been avoiding, as Lee's security

00:04:08.829 --> 00:04:13.629
monitors show the other two creatures known
to inhabit the area racing toward the farmhouse.

00:04:13.629 --> 00:04:17.560
But Evelyn's ready this time and gives her
daughter a reassuring smile as she cocks the

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.340
shotgun and the movie cuts to credits, sending
the audience out of the theater without releasing

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.120
their adrenaline high.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.120
The next generation

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.430
Evelyn's pregnancy and labor are a driving
source of tension for most of A Quiet Place,

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.660
and it's not just to harvest the audience's
anxieties.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:37.590
A major theme of the film is the struggle
to survive and adapt to some kind of normalcy

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.110
in the midst of horrific societal changes.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.090
That's why the invasion occurs before the
story begins and the rebellion against the

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.330
monsters is saved for after its ending.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:50.400
Evelyn and Lee's newborn baby serves as a
symbol for the belief that life can go on.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.229
Children will be born who never knew life
before the quiet.

00:04:53.229 --> 00:04:55.840
"Who are we, if we can't protect them?"

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:59.840
Regan, Marcus, and the baby at their mother's
side in the film's final moments represent

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.470
what the story is all about: the future.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.009
Thanks for watching!

